# tools/ales_stereo_preset_witness.rish — a keeper loads a named effect chain by name and hears it over BOTH channels of a
# stereo master, verify-before-trust (ALES220).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus · the creative suite) · waymark ALES · rung ALES220.
# Design read: active-designing/20260815-133213_fill-ales220-lotus-stereo-preset.md
# Idiom kin: lotus/preset.rye (ALES219, from_name + build) · lotus/stereo_render.rye (ALES218, the balanced render) · lotus/
# pan.rye (ALES10, the StereoClip). This rung is the mono→stereo twin of the preset surface: the named preset widened to the
# second channel, inventing no new effect, check, or name.
#
# lotus/stereo_preset.rye loads a preset by name and renders it over both channels through the balanced stereo render. The
# selftest proves: each catalog preset rendered by name decodes byte-for-byte on each channel to the same preset applied by hand
# (the named-stereo law); a named stereo preset is the same preset rendered mono per channel (the independent-channel law); an
# unknown name refuses UnknownPreset before the master is read, both channels unchanged (the unknown law); every render leaves
# the two channels equal length (the balance law); a small container refuses OutputTooSmall, both channels untouched (the atomic
# law) — build is total, so no preset ever refuses for BadRange. A byte container only — no real file opened, no DAC, no
# network, no keys, no funds, no real device.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/ales_stereo_preset_witness.rish

say "ales-stereo-preset: Language EN — ALES220 is the mono→stereo twin of the preset surface: a keeper loads a named chain by name and hears it over both channels of a stereo master, reusing ALES219's from_name and build and ALES218's balanced render verbatim."
say "ales-stereo-preset: Style Radiant — the named-stereo law (byte-for-byte on each channel to a hand render), the independent-channel law (two mono renders sharing one container), and the unknown law (a stranger name refuses before the master is read) each named and proven."
say "ales-stereo-preset: Lens TAME — build is total over the shared length so a named preset never refuses for BadRange and both channels leave equal length by construction; the only faults are the container's, each refusing before a sample moves; siloed to lotus/, no real file, no DAC, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/stereo_preset"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/stereo_preset.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-stereo-preset: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/stereo_preset.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-stereo-preset: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-stereo-preset: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-stereo-preset' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-stereo-preset: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-stereo-preset line"

say "ales-stereo-preset: GREEN — a named preset renders over both channels of a stereo master, byte-for-byte to two mono renders sharing one interleaved container; the render+preset family now stands whole for mono and stereo. The next Lotus crux can grow the catalog or let a keeper save their own chain as a named preset."
